{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792893586,"nonce":"b14oRCu4QjZz+mYry3GvyzUMBzw=","title":"Hot-reload object room is added to every HOBJ instance, std classes included","message":"hlp_alloc_obj adds OBJECT_ROOM (64 bytes by default) to every HOBJ instance, so String, the Array classes and haxe.io.Bytes carry it although a reload never changes their layout. Reported by the caribou session, which turns reload on by default and calls reserve_object_room() for plugin classes: on a probe of 10000 each of Bytes, 10-float arrays and small objects after Gc.major(), marked lines were 17.0 MB with room 64, 13.8 MB with ASH_RELOAD_ROOM=0, 12.5 MB for plain ash with no reload. ChimpMonk's editor shows about 1.32x against ash (being confirmed).\n\nWhat reload can use: fields.rs only adds a field to a class that nothing extends, so room on a class with subclasses is never used, and the std and runtime classes of a program are not the ones a user edits.\n\nhlp_alloc_obj can decide per type: it has the type, and object_tail(t) and the drop set already key on the type address. The decision has to be fixed at the type's first allocation, because the layout is.\n\nOptions:\n- No room for classes with subclasses (known from the program's type table, at layout time).\n- No room for std/runtime classes (String, Array*, Bytes, hl.* and haxe.* internals), by name or by being defined in the std part of the program.\n- A smaller default than 64, since a field is 8 bytes; ASH_RELOAD_ROOM already sets it.\n- Per-class room sized to what a reload could add.\n\nCheck against: hot reload tests that add fields (reload slice 4), and a heap-size probe like the caribou one.","files":null}]}